  "articleBody": "Altering structural framing leaves no margin for guesswork. Even minor framing errors can compromise an entire floor system or cause ceiling cracking. If you are preparing to hire a framing contractor, keeping an eye out for these frequent mistakes will save you serious headaches.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid:\n- Undersized Headers: Installing headers without verifying code span tables or engineered plans causes headers to sag over wide spans. Always confirm sizing meets structural loads.\n- Missing King or Jack Studs: Omitting proper bearing support beneath headers transfers weight unevenly. Ensure every header rests firmly on designated jack studs.\n- Inadequate Anchoring: Failing to anchor bottom plates securely into the floor system or foundation allows lateral movement. Fastener schedules must suit the subfloor or slab.\n- Interrupted Bracing: Omitting continuous wall bracing reduces resistance to lateral forces. Keep bracing paths continuous across framed sections.\n- Skipping Load Path Verification: Tearing out or adjusting studs before verifying what rests above can lead to sudden ceiling drops. Temporary shoring must stay in place until new members are secured.\n- Misaligned Stud Spacing: Inconsistent stud centers complicate drywall hanging and insulation fit. Stick strictly to standard layout spacing.\n\nIf your renovation requires modifying a load-bearing wall, reach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 for dependable, hands-on structural framing expertise.",
